      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Extracts crew/staff service failures (rudeness, inattentiveness, inefficiency) from review text as a candidate cause of low ratings and non-recommendation. This is a plausible manipulable treatment whose effect on the outcome is being attributed. Not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "aircraft_modernization",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Aircraft age/condition (dated, modern, worn) plausibly affects both perceived crew/product experience and the overall rating. It is surfaced from text, not in the query. However it could also act as a parallel treatment; treated as a common contextual driver here."
    },
    {
      "name": "price_value_alignment",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Perceived value-for-money is largely a downstream judgment that sits on the causal path between service/product quality and the overall rating/recommendation. Adjusting for it would block part of the very effect being attributed, so it is a mediator rather than a genuine confounder."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["crew_service_quality_issues"],
  "confounders": [
    {"name": "aircraft_modernization", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.5}
  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.35,
  "rationale": "A clear treatment (crew service quality issues) is surfaced from the review text, satisfying part (a). For part (b), only aircraft_modernization is a candidate confounder and it is genuinely surfaced from data rather than copied from the query, but its status as a common cause of BOTH the crew-service treatment and the outcome is weak/ambiguous (it may act as a separate treatment). The remaining added column, price_value_alignment, is a mediator on the causal path to the outcome and adjusting for it would bias the attribution. Overall the set gestures at causal estimation but provides no strong, unambiguous common-cause confounder, so confounder quality is low."
